# AppImage build outputs
dist/*.AppImage

# Smoke-test failure debris. `pytest_runtest_makereport` (tests/smoke/conftest.py)
# writes a `.state.json` dump and a `.trowel.log` here ONLY when a test fails, so
# a committed file records a failure on somebody's machine at some point: nothing
# reads them, no test depends on them, and a green run leaves stale ones in place
# looking current. They also embed absolute paths.
#
# CI already does this the right way -- .github/workflows/ci.yml has an "Upload
# smoke artifacts on failure" step pointing at this directory, which works
# whether or not it is tracked.
tests/smoke/artifacts/
